  "id": "COMPOUND:550 - DISEASE:886",
  "verbalization": "Carbamazepine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Double Outlet Right Ventricle through a mechanism involving microRNA 3169. The evidence suggests that carbamazepine affects microRNA 3169, which in turn contributes to the development of this cardiac condition. The consistent scores across three distinct paths reinforce the reliability of this relationship, indicating a robust biological pathway. The involvement of microRNA 3169 in the pathophysiology of Double Outlet Right Ventricle highlights a potential therapeutic target, as modulating this miRNA could offer a novel approach to treating the condition. The integration of these findings underscores the role of miRNA regulation in cardiovascular development, suggesting that carbamazepine may exert its effects through this molecular mechanism.",
